WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.180 --> 00:00:02.210
(phone ringing)

00:00:02.210 --> 00:00:03.043
- [Wes] Hello?

00:00:03.043 --> 00:00:04.100
- Hey, Wes, what's going on, man.

00:00:04.100 --> 00:00:05.210
It's Karamo.

00:00:05.210 --> 00:00:06.410
- [Wes] What's going on, man?

00:00:06.410 --> 00:00:07.500
- I was thinking of a way

00:00:07.500 --> 00:00:08.420
that I could help you,

00:00:08.420 --> 00:00:09.710
but I need your blessing.

00:00:09.710 --> 00:00:11.530
- [Wes] It's been granted.

00:00:11.530 --> 00:00:13.330
- That night is critical

00:00:13.330 --> 00:00:14.990
in who you are as a man,

00:00:14.990 --> 00:00:16.240
but there's still little holes

00:00:16.240 --> 00:00:17.390
for you that I'm noticing

00:00:17.390 --> 00:00:18.830
that, like, have to get fixed

00:00:18.830 --> 00:00:20.300
and get plugged.

00:00:20.300 --> 00:00:21.970
So I've set up an opportunity

00:00:21.970 --> 00:00:23.660
for Wesley to meet Maurice,

00:00:23.660 --> 00:00:25.151
the man who shot him.

00:00:25.151 --> 00:00:25.984
(instrumental music)

00:00:25.984 --> 00:00:26.817
- [Wesley] I became a bad boy

00:00:26.817 --> 00:00:28.300
at a young age.

00:00:28.300 --> 00:00:30.500
I remember wanting to fit in,

00:00:30.500 --> 00:00:32.450
wanting to look like everybody else.

00:00:32.450 --> 00:00:34.337
And being inspired and motivated

00:00:34.337 --> 00:00:36.741
by the only role models I could,

00:00:36.741 --> 00:00:39.386
which were drug dealers in my community.

00:00:39.386 --> 00:00:41.300
I was gonna live my life

00:00:41.300 --> 00:00:43.050
as reckless as I could

00:00:43.050 --> 00:00:45.060
because I knew that eventually

00:00:45.060 --> 00:00:46.040
I was gonna die

00:00:46.040 --> 00:00:47.404
or I was gonna go to jail.

00:00:47.404 --> 00:00:48.280
(police sirens)

00:00:48.280 --> 00:00:50.170
Five days after my 24th birthday

00:00:50.170 --> 00:00:51.500
I was shot multiple times

00:00:51.500 --> 00:00:52.410
in my abdomen.

00:00:52.410 --> 00:00:53.790
- They turned to me

00:00:54.750 --> 00:00:56.120
and said

00:00:56.120 --> 00:00:57.420
he's paralyzed

00:00:57.420 --> 00:00:58.670
from the waist down.

00:00:58.670 --> 00:01:00.370
That was the worst day of my life.

00:01:01.320 --> 00:01:03.190
Two years of bedridden,

00:01:03.190 --> 00:01:04.983
just up a couple of hours a day.

00:01:08.460 --> 00:01:10.240
- I cried so much.

00:01:10.240 --> 00:01:11.560
I remember many nights

00:01:11.560 --> 00:01:13.110
of just beating my legs up

00:01:13.110 --> 00:01:15.510
because I just thought
they were worthless.

00:01:15.510 --> 00:01:16.803
I hated myself.

00:01:19.850 --> 00:01:21.300
You gotta always think, like,

00:01:21.300 --> 00:01:22.760
you'll be looking at a man

00:01:22.760 --> 00:01:25.570
that tried to take your life.

00:01:25.570 --> 00:01:27.580
I just don't want my emotions

00:01:27.580 --> 00:01:28.883
to get over me.

00:01:31.030 --> 00:01:32.740
- Like, people assume that forgiveness

00:01:32.740 --> 00:01:34.200
is a destination,

00:01:34.200 --> 00:01:35.360
not realizing it's a journey

00:01:35.360 --> 00:01:37.020
that continues on throughout your life.

00:01:37.020 --> 00:01:38.620
- Right.

00:01:38.620 --> 00:01:40.593
I feel like I can handle it.

00:01:42.519 --> 00:01:45.269
(rhythmic music)

00:01:55.919 --> 00:01:59.002
(background chatter)

00:02:04.297 --> 00:02:05.480
What's up with it man?

00:02:05.480 --> 00:02:06.521
- How's it going.

00:02:06.521 --> 00:02:07.460
- [Karamo] Karamo.

00:02:07.460 --> 00:02:08.293
- [Maurice] Karamo?

00:02:08.293 --> 00:02:09.126
- [Karamo] Yeah.
- [Maurice] Maurice.

00:02:09.126 --> 00:02:10.044
- [Karamo] Nice to meet you, man.

00:02:10.044 --> 00:02:10.940
- [Maurice] You too.

00:02:10.940 --> 00:02:11.880
- First of all, thank you again

00:02:11.880 --> 00:02:13.000
for you being here.

00:02:13.000 --> 00:02:15.090
Thank you for you being
willing to do this.

00:02:15.090 --> 00:02:19.195
I just am here to help you
all navigate this coversation,

00:02:19.195 --> 00:02:20.980
but this is your time

00:02:22.540 --> 00:02:25.260
to sort of ask whatever
questions, get clarity.

00:02:25.260 --> 00:02:26.610
You kind of don't know why

00:02:26.610 --> 00:02:28.060
and what happened that night.

00:02:29.600 --> 00:02:33.323
- That day, I only seen you for a second.

00:02:34.350 --> 00:02:36.930
I was literally walking
back to my car leaving.

00:02:36.930 --> 00:02:39.050
We never had, like, a conversation

00:02:39.050 --> 00:02:41.163
or, like, an altercation.

00:02:42.600 --> 00:02:44.529
- You don't believe that

00:02:44.529 --> 00:02:45.362
(clears throat)

00:02:45.362 --> 00:02:48.190
you've done anything to
warrant what happened?

00:02:48.190 --> 00:02:51.660
- No, like, I mean, I just
know who I was before.

00:02:51.660 --> 00:02:52.980
- I don't want to go back and forth

00:02:52.980 --> 00:02:55.610
to make it, like, a whose fault this was,

00:02:55.610 --> 00:02:56.443
whose fault that was.

00:02:56.443 --> 00:02:57.490
I don't want to do that.

00:02:57.490 --> 00:02:58.540
To get you kind of clarity

00:02:58.540 --> 00:03:00.640
on my perspective of what happened.

00:03:00.640 --> 00:03:03.400
When I get there, I see your partner

00:03:03.400 --> 00:03:05.130
and your woman at the time,

00:03:05.130 --> 00:03:07.720
or whatever like that arguing.

00:03:07.720 --> 00:03:09.830
- So I understand that my actions,

00:03:09.830 --> 00:03:11.450
and my feelings, and my emotions

00:03:11.450 --> 00:03:13.350
probably took the best of me that day.

00:03:14.210 --> 00:03:16.063
But it was still more or less, like,

00:03:17.250 --> 00:03:18.293
why you?

00:03:19.150 --> 00:03:21.720
- I see you bucking up to my cousin,

00:03:21.720 --> 00:03:22.553
you know what I'm saying.

00:03:22.553 --> 00:03:24.460
And he told me that you had a pistol.

00:03:24.460 --> 00:03:26.190
Your partner, I see his pistol.

00:03:26.190 --> 00:03:28.200
He got a 30-round magazine hanging out.

00:03:28.200 --> 00:03:29.513
And I seen him back and forth going.

00:03:29.513 --> 00:03:31.907
And I am like, "Damn
all this over a bitch."

00:03:32.770 --> 00:03:34.778
That's when you started
coming over towards me.

00:03:34.778 --> 00:03:35.611
- Yeah

00:03:35.611 --> 00:03:36.444
- You know how the streets are,

00:03:36.444 --> 00:03:37.560
you know, I can't see yours.

00:03:37.560 --> 00:03:39.970
In my mind you got the pistol too.

00:03:39.970 --> 00:03:40.827
I'm like, "Man look,

00:03:40.827 --> 00:03:41.747
"I'm not going for that.

00:03:41.747 --> 00:03:42.837
"I can't, you know what I'm saying,

00:03:42.837 --> 00:03:44.670
"risk me getting shot or getting,"

00:03:44.670 --> 00:03:46.290
you know what I'm saying, so

00:03:46.290 --> 00:03:47.707
what happened, happened.

00:03:50.070 --> 00:03:53.133
- It's crazy to hear it now.

00:03:54.560 --> 00:03:58.480
We lived in a place where we all strap.

00:03:58.480 --> 00:04:00.090
You know, we don't care
as long as we trying

00:04:00.090 --> 00:04:01.740
to protect somebody that we love.

00:04:05.600 --> 00:04:08.170
I could understand why
you did what you did.

00:04:08.170 --> 00:04:10.320
If it was the other way around,

00:04:10.320 --> 00:04:12.450
I probably would react
the same way you did.

00:04:12.450 --> 00:04:14.900
- I didn't imagine you seeing
it from that prospective.

00:04:14.900 --> 00:04:18.103
Like, it was no malice in my heart.

00:04:19.200 --> 00:04:21.940
- [Karamo] Wes, do you need an apology.

00:04:21.940 --> 00:04:25.453
- I don't think it's
necessary for an apology.

00:04:27.190 --> 00:04:29.670
I would prefer not you to feel sorry.

00:04:29.670 --> 00:04:30.503
I thank you

00:04:31.860 --> 00:04:33.793
for me being, like, in this position.

00:04:35.440 --> 00:04:37.950
I don't even feel bad energy from you.

00:04:37.950 --> 00:04:39.008
- That's crazy.

00:04:39.008 --> 00:04:39.841
I was thinking the same thing.

00:04:39.841 --> 00:04:41.630
I'm like, "Man."

00:04:41.630 --> 00:04:46.000
- I'm actually empowered by
the life I was given that day.

00:04:46.000 --> 00:04:48.150
I've had a lot of time to grow.

00:04:48.150 --> 00:04:49.800
- I'm definitely in a better space,

00:04:49.800 --> 00:04:53.300
you know, just striving to
be the man I know I can be.

00:04:53.300 --> 00:04:55.090
- We are two black men

00:04:55.090 --> 00:04:58.150
and we're doing something that

00:04:59.320 --> 00:05:00.570
they don't want us to do

00:05:02.075 --> 00:05:04.260
and that is forgive each other,

00:05:04.260 --> 00:05:06.210
but also uplift each other.

00:05:06.210 --> 00:05:08.060
I found purpose in my situation

00:05:08.060 --> 00:05:10.220
and it seems like you did too.

00:05:10.220 --> 00:05:13.480
- I just plan on doing great
things from here on out.

00:05:13.480 --> 00:05:15.980
Hopefully we can both
do some great things.

00:05:15.980 --> 00:05:18.730
- Hey man, I see we can do
it probably together, man.

00:05:18.730 --> 00:05:19.780
- It's real.

00:05:19.780 --> 00:05:21.290
- I agree with you.

00:05:21.290 --> 00:05:22.900
I have a feeling this
is just the beginning

00:05:22.900 --> 00:05:23.840
of a bigger purpose

00:05:23.840 --> 00:05:25.790
that I don't even think y'all knew.

00:05:25.790 --> 00:05:27.278
- Hey man, I'm with it.

00:05:27.278 --> 00:05:28.430
- Appreciate you, bro.
- Thank you, bro.

00:05:28.430 --> 00:05:29.930
- My son.
- I appreciate you.

00:05:32.400 --> 00:05:33.500
- [Wes] Wow.

00:05:33.500 --> 00:05:34.690
- [Karamo] How was that, good?

00:05:34.690 --> 00:05:36.090
- Wow.

00:05:36.090 --> 00:05:37.970
It was really really liberating

00:05:37.970 --> 00:05:42.360
and I'm, like, having
all these mixed emotions.

00:05:42.360 --> 00:05:45.660
Like, I looked at a man that shot me

00:05:45.660 --> 00:05:46.592
and told him, "Thank you."

00:05:46.592 --> 00:05:47.425
- Mm.

00:05:47.425 --> 00:05:48.950
- And now I can be the Wesley Hamilton

00:05:48.950 --> 00:05:50.437
that I always wanted to be.

00:05:50.437 --> 00:05:51.735
- [Karomo] Yeah.

00:05:51.735 --> 00:05:54.402
(both laughing)

